# =============================================================================
# COMMITTED TEMPLATE - documents the NAMES only.
# Copy to .env and fill it in. NEVER put a real value in this file.
#
# ⚠️ .env is gitignored and must stay that way. Secrets that reach a commit are
#    in history forever: they have to be rotated AND the repo re-created without
#    its history before it can be shared. See config/env/requireEnv.ts.
#
# ⚠️ SINGLE-QUOTE ANY VALUE CONTAINING '#'. dotenv ends an unquoted value at the
#    first '#' anywhere in it - a password with one in the middle silently
#    becomes a shorter password, and you debug an auth failure that isn't one.
# =============================================================================

# --- EVERYTHING BELOW IS COMMENTED OUT AND OPTIONAL. It documents what a real
#     app's suite tends to need - uncomment what yours uses, delete the rest.
#     With auth.strategy "none" and testData.provider "none", a suite needs no
#     secrets at all. A worked example is on the `demo` branch.

# --- Credentials the suite signs in with, if your app has auth.
#     ⚠️ A DEDICATED TEST ACCOUNT, never a real user's.
# APP_USERNAME=
# APP_PASSWORD=

# --- Your test-data provider, if you plug one in (test/support/testData.ts).
# DB_SERVER=
# DB_USER=
# DB_PASSWORD=

# --- Device / binary overrides. All optional - config/app.ts holds the defaults.
# ANDROID_APP_PATH=./apps/YourApp.apk
# IOS_APP_PATH=./apps/YourApp.app
# IOS_DEVICE_NAME=iPhone 16e
# ANDROID_DEVICE_NAME=Android Emulator

# --- Run knobs. See docs/architecture/performance.md before changing TIMEOUT_SCALE.
# PLATFORM=android
# TIMEOUT_SCALE=1
# ISOLATED=false
